    "bottomLine": "The right cordless for a small home, a second floor or a first purchase where cost matters most.",
    "description": "Eufy, known for its robot vacuums, sells the HomeVac S11 Go as a no-nonsense, affordable cordless stick. It converts to a handheld for stairs, upholstery and cars, shows its mode on a small display, and uses a removable battery. It will not match a flagship on carpet depth or filtration, and owners with big houses or heavy pet shedding will likely outgrow it. But for hard floors, light carpet and routine daily pickups, it covers the essentials at a sensible cost. As with every brand here, check the specific listing for current runtime and accessory details."
  },
  {
    "id": "roborock-dyad-pro",
    "name": "Roborock Dyad Pro Wet-Dry Vacuum",
    "category": "Cordless Wet-Dry",
    "badge": "Best for Hard Floors and Spills",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Vacuums and mops in one pass on sealed hard floors",
      "Self-cleaning dock and separate clean and dirty water tanks",
      "Handles wet messes that a dry stick would smear",
      "Self-propelled design reduces pushing effort",
      "Good fit for homes that are mostly tile, vinyl or laminate"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "A hard-floor tool: it is not meant to replace a vacuum on carpet or rugs",
      "Larger and heavier than a conventional stick, with water to fill and empty"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Choose it as the hard-floor machine in a home that already has a lightweight stick or robot for carpet.",
    "description": "The Dyad Pro is a different animal from the other sticks here. It is a cordless wet-dry cleaner that picks up dry debris and wet spills while mopping the floor in the same pass, then cleans its own roller at the dock. For tile, vinyl, sealed wood and laminate homes, especially those with kids and pets, it changes the routine of vacuum-then-mop into a single trip. It is not a carpet machine, and it asks you to manage clean and dirty water tanks. Roborock sells related Dyad variants, so verify the model and what it is rated for on your flooring."
  },
  {
    "id": "bissell-pet-hair-eraser-hand-vac",
    "name": "Bissell Pet Hair Eraser Cordless Hand Vacuum",
    "category": "Handheld, Pet Hair",
    "badge": "Best Handheld for Pets",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Compact handheld that suits couches, stairs, car seats and pet beds",
      "Motorized tool designed to lift pet hair from upholstery",
      "Lightweight enough to hang on a hook and grab for quick messes",
      "Costs far less than a full stick",
      "Washable filter that cuts running costs"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "A supplement to a main vacuum, not a replacement for one",
      "Small dust bin and short runtime compared with a full stick"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A low-cost add-on for pet owners whose main frustration is hair on furniture and in the car.",
    "description": "Not everyone needs a full stick vacuum, and plenty of households just want something light for the sofa, the stairs and the back seat. Bissell’s Pet Hair Eraser hand vacuum is built for that job, with a motorized upholstery tool aimed at pet hair and a washable filter that saves on replacements. It is a supplement rather than a main vacuum, because the bin is small and the runtime short, but for sofa and car duty it is difficult to beat on cost. Bissell sells several similarly named versions, so check the exact model and what tools come with it."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Cordless Vacuums",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-cordless-vacuum/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long do cordless vacuums last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The motor usually outlasts the battery. Owners commonly report that lithium-ion packs lose noticeable capacity after a few years of regular use. With a removable battery and cleaned filters, a good cordless can run for many years, whereas a built-in battery often sets the machine's practical lifespan."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a cordless vacuum as powerful as a corded one?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On paper, corded uprights often deliver more sustained suction for the price because they are not limited by a battery. Modern cordless sticks come close for everyday cleaning, especially in boost mode, but they cannot match unlimited runtime. For small and medium homes, the convenience usually outweighs the difference."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often should I replace the filter?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Follow the manufacturer's guidance, which for most washable filters means rinsing roughly once a month and replacing every year or so, depending on use. If suction drops or the machine smells musty, check the filter first, and always let it dry completely before refitting."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which cordless vacuum is best for pet hair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Look for an anti-tangle brushroll, a sealed filter and a bin large enough for your home. The Shark Vertex and Dyson V15 Detect are strong candidates, and a small handheld such as the Bissell is useful for furniture. Confirm each model's current specifications before you buy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a cordless vacuum replace a robot vacuum?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "They do different jobs. A robot maintains floors day to day while you are out, but it struggles with stairs, edges and deep carpet. A cordless stick handles those jobs. Many homes use both, and our comparison of the two explains how to divide the cleaning between them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are expensive cordless vacuums worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on your home. Premium sticks add sensing, better filtration, longer-lasting batteries and better build quality, which matter for allergies, pets and heavy use. For a small apartment with mostly hard floors, a mid-range or budget stick often does the job just as well at a lower cost."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use a cordless vacuum on wet spills?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most cordless stick vacuums are dry-only, and water can damage the motor and battery. If you regularly deal with spills, choose a machine designed for wet and dry use, such as the Roborock Dyad Pro, or use a wet-capable shop vacuum. Check the manual for what your model supports."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Appliances",
    tags: [
      "best cordless vacuum",
      "cordless vacuum",
      "cordless stick vacuum",
      "best cordless vacuum for pet hair",
      "cordless vacuum cleaner"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Buyer's Guide 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Cordless <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Vacuums</span> for Every Home
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Seven cordless vacuums worth shortlisting, with a plain-English guide to runtime, batteries, filtration and pet hair.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#dyson-v15-detect"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Jump to the Buying Guide
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Shaheer Ali Khan</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Consumer Product Testing &amp; Materials Performance Specialist</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="19.4k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#buying-guide" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. Cordless Vacuum Buying Guide</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Our 7 Top Picks Reviewed</a>
          <a href="#runtime-power" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Runtime vs Power</a>
          <a href="#batteries" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Batteries</a>
          <a href="#suction-filtration" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Suction & Filtration</a>
          <a href="#pet-hair-floors" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Pet Hair & Floors</a>
          <a href="#weight-bin-attachments" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Weight, Bin & Attachments</a>
          <a href="#cordless-vs-others" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Cordless vs Other Vacuums</a>
          <a href="#cost-ownership" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Cost of Ownership</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A cordless vacuum is the cleaning tool most households reach for every day, which makes the wrong one an expensive daily irritation. The right pick depends less on the biggest suction number and more on the runtime you get in the mode you will use, a battery you can replace, filtration that suits your home, and a weight your wrist tolerates. Here are seven we would shortlist, and how to choose between them.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="buying-guide" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Cordless Vacuum Buying Guide: What Actually Matters
          </h2>

          <p>
            Most people shop for a cordless vacuum by comparing suction numbers, and that is the least useful place to start. Suction ratings are measured under conditions that rarely match your living room, they are quoted in different units by different brands, and they say nothing about whether the machine will still be running when you reach the back bedroom. A better shortlist begins with four questions: what floors you have, whether you have pets, how large the space is, and who will be pushing the machine.
          </p>

          <p>
            Floor type decides the head you want. A soft roller suits hard floors and picks up fine dust without scattering it, while a bristle brushroll agitates carpet fibres to release embedded dirt. Dual-purpose heads try to do both, and the best of them manage reasonably well on a mixed home. If you have mostly hard floors, a lighter machine with a soft roller is likely to serve you better than a heavy carpet-focused one.
          </p>

          <p>
            Home size and clutter shape the battery question. A small flat or a single floor can be done on one charge in a mid power mode, while a two-storey house with several rugs may push a battery past its limits. Consider whether you will clean in one session or in short bursts, because a vacuum on a wall dock that you grab for two minutes at a time has very different requirements from one you use once a week.
          </p>

          <p>
            Finally, think about the people. Weight, trigger style and balance matter more over a year of use than any spec on the box. A machine that is slightly less powerful but that you actually enjoy picking up will clean more often and get your floors cleaner than a powerful one that lives in the closet. Keep those four questions in mind as you read the picks below, and use the later sections to dig into each trade-off.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The 7 Best Cordless Vacuums in 2026, Ranked by Who They Suit
          </h2>

          <p>
            These are the seven cordless vacuums we would shortlist, chosen from manufacturer specifications and the pattern of what owners commonly report, not from bench tests of our own. Specs change between model years, so confirm the details on the current listing before you buy. The Check Price buttons are affiliate links: if you purchase through them we earn a commission at no extra cost to you, and it never changes which products make the list.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-[#FF4500] text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-black">
                      {index + 1}
                    </span>
                    {productImages[product.id] && (
                      <img
                        src={productImages[product.id]}
                        alt={product.name}
                        loading="lazy"
                        width="40"
                        height="40"
                        class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-white object-contain p-1 shrink-0"
                      />
                    )}
                    <div>
                      <h3 class="text-white font-black text-lg leading-snug m-0"><span class="block text-[#38BDF8] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 sm:hidden">{product.badge}</span>{product.name}</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#38BDF8]/20 text-[#38BDF8] px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold hidden sm:block">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  {product.rating && product.reviewCount && (
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
                    <div class="flex text-yellow-400">
                      {[...Array(5)].map((_, i) => (
                        <svg
                          class={`w-4 h-4 ${i < Math.floor(product.rating) ? "fill-current" : "text-gray-200"}`}
                          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                          viewBox="0 0 20 20"
